              - emphasis:
                - generic: result
                - generic: =
                - generic: None
              - text: )
            - definition:
              - paragraph:
                - text: Block for
                - emphasis: delay
                - text: seconds.
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - emphasis: result
                - text: is provided, it is returned to the caller when the coroutine completes.
              - paragraph:
                - code: sleep()
                - text: always suspends the current task, allowing other tasks to run.
              - paragraph: Setting the delay to 0 provides an optimized path to allow other tasks to run. This can be used by long-running functions to avoid blocking the event loop for the full duration of the function call.
              - paragraph: "Example of coroutine displaying the current date every second for 5 seconds:"
              - generic: "import asyncio import datetime as dt async def display_date(): loop = asyncio.get_running_loop() end_time = loop.time() + 5.0 while True: print(dt.datetime.now()) if (loop.time() + 1.0) >= end_time: break await asyncio.sleep(1) asyncio.run(display_date())"
              - paragraph:
                - text: "Changed in version 3.10: Removed the"
                - emphasis: loop
                - text: parameter.
              - paragraph:
                - text: "Changed in version 3.13: Raises"
                - link [ref=f83e517]:
                  - /url: ../builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError
                  - code: ValueError
                - text: if
                - emphasis: delay
                - text: is
                - link [ref=f83e520]:
                  - /url: math.html#math.nan
                  - code: nan
                - text: .
        - generic:
          - heading [level=2] [ref=f83e523]:
            - link "Running tasks concurrently" [ref=f83e524]:
              - /url: "#id8"
          - generic:
            - term:
              - emphasis: awaitable
              - generic: asyncio.
              - generic: gather
              - text: (
              - emphasis:
                - generic: "*"
                - generic: aws
              - emphasis:
                - generic: return_exceptions
                - generic: =
                - generic: "False"
              - text: )
            - definition:
              - paragraph:
                - text: Run
                - link "awaitable objects" [ref=f83e539]:
                  - /url: "#asyncio-awaitables"
                - text: in the
                - emphasis: aws
                - text: sequence
                - emphasis: concurrently
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: If any awaitable in
                - emphasis: aws
                - text: is a coroutine, it is automatically scheduled as a Task.
              - paragraph:
                - text: If all awaitables are completed successfully, the result is an aggregate list of returned values. The order of result values corresponds to the order of awaitables in
                - emphasis: aws
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - emphasis: return_exceptions
                - text: is
                - code: "False"
                - text: (default), the first raised exception is immediately propagated to the task that awaits on
                - code: gather()
                - text: . Other awaitables in the
                - emphasis: aws
                - text: sequence
                - strong: won’t be cancelled
                - text: and will continue to run.
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - emphasis: return_exceptions
                - text: is
                - code: "True"
                - text: ", exceptions are treated the same as successful results, and aggregated in the result list."
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - code: gather()
                - text: is
                - emphasis: cancelled
                - text: ", all submitted awaitables (that have not completed yet) are also"
                - emphasis: cancelled
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: If any Task or Future from the
                - emphasis: aws
                - text: sequence is
                - emphasis: cancelled
                - text: ", it is treated as if it raised"
                - link [ref=f83e562]:
                  - /url: asyncio-exceptions.html#asyncio.CancelledError
                  - code: CancelledError
                - text: – the
                - code: gather()
                - text: call is
                - strong: not
                - text: cancelled in this case. This is to prevent the cancellation of one submitted Task/Future to cause other Tasks/Futures to be cancelled.
              - generic:
                - paragraph: "Note:"
                - paragraph:
                  - text: A new alternative to create and run tasks concurrently and wait for their completion is
                  - link [ref=f83e569]:
                    - /url: "#asyncio.TaskGroup"
                    - code: asyncio.TaskGroup
                  - text: .
                  - emphasis: TaskGroup
                  - text: provides stronger safety guarantees than
                  - emphasis: gather
                  - text: "for scheduling a nesting of subtasks: if a task (or a subtask, a task scheduled by a task) raises an exception,"
                  - emphasis: TaskGroup
                  - text: will, while
                  - emphasis: gather
                  - text: will not, cancel the remaining scheduled tasks.
              - paragraph: "Example:"
              - generic: "import asyncio async def factorial(name, number): f = 1 for i in range(2, number + 1): print(f\"Task {name}: Compute factorial({number}), currently i={i}...\") await asyncio.sleep(1) f *= i print(f\"Task {name}: factorial({number}) = {f}\") return f async def main(): # Schedule three calls *concurrently*: L = await asyncio.gather( factorial(\"A\", 2), factorial(\"B\", 3), factorial(\"C\", 4), ) print(L) asyncio.run(main()) # Expected output: # # Task A: Compute factorial(2), currently i=2... # Task B: Compute factorial(3), currently i=2... # Task C: Compute factorial(4), currently i=2... # Task A: factorial(2) = 2 # Task B: Compute factorial(3), currently i=3... # Task C: Compute factorial(4), currently i=3... # Task B: factorial(3) = 6 # Task C: Compute factorial(4), currently i=4... # Task C: factorial(4) = 24 # [2, 6, 24]"
              - generic:
                - paragraph: "Note:"
                - paragraph:
                  - text: If
                  - emphasis: return_exceptions
                  - text: is false, cancelling gather() after it has been marked done won’t cancel any submitted awaitables. For instance, gather can be marked done after propagating an exception to the caller, therefore, calling
                  - code: gather.cancel()
                  - text: after catching an exception (raised by one of the awaitables) from gather won’t cancel any other awaitables.
              - paragraph:
                - text: "Changed in version 3.7: If the"
                - emphasis: gather
                - text: itself is cancelled, the cancellation is propagated regardless of
                - emphasis: return_exceptions
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: "Changed in version 3.10: Removed the"
                - emphasis: loop
                - text: parameter.
              - paragraph: "Deprecated since version 3.10: Deprecation warning is emitted if no positional arguments are provided or not all positional arguments are Future-like objects and there is no running event loop."
        - generic:
          - heading [level=2] [ref=f83e594]:
            - link "Eager task factory" [ref=f83e595]:
              - /url: "#id9"
          - generic:
            - term:
              - generic: asyncio.
              - generic: eager_task_factory
              - text: (
              - emphasis:
                - generic: loop
              - emphasis:
                - generic: coro
              - emphasis:
                - generic "Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)": "*"
              - emphasis:
                - generic: name
                - generic: =
                - generic: None
              - emphasis:
                - generic: context
                - generic: =
                - generic: None
              - text: )
            - definition:
              - paragraph: A task factory for eager task execution.
              - paragraph:
                - text: When using this factory (via
                - link [ref=f83e618]:
                  - /url: asyncio-eventloop.html#asyncio.loop.set_task_factory
                  - code: loop.set_task_factory(asyncio.eager_task_factory)
                - text: ), coroutines begin execution synchronously during
                - link [ref=f83e620]:
                  - /url: "#asyncio.Task"
                  - code: Task
                - text: construction. Tasks are only scheduled on the event loop if they block. This can be a performance improvement as the overhead of loop scheduling is avoided for coroutines that complete synchronously.
              - paragraph: A common example where this is beneficial is coroutines which employ caching or memoization to avoid actual I/O when possible.
              - generic:
                - paragraph: "Note:"
                - paragraph: Immediate execution of the coroutine is a semantic change. If the coroutine returns or raises, the task is never scheduled to the event loop. If the coroutine execution blocks, the task is scheduled to the event loop. This change may introduce behavior changes to existing applications. For example, the application’s task execution order is likely to change.
              - paragraph: Added in version 3.12.
          - generic:
            - term:
              - generic: asyncio.
              - generic: create_eager_task_factory
              - text: (
              - emphasis:
                - generic: custom_task_constructor
              - text: )
            - definition:
