            - definition:
              - paragraph:
                - text: Protect an
                - link "awaitable object" [ref=f83e666]:
                  - /url: "#asyncio-awaitables"
                - text: from being
                - link [ref=f83e667]:
                  - /url: "#asyncio.Task.cancel"
                  - code: cancelled
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - emphasis: aw
                - text: is a coroutine it is automatically scheduled as a Task.
              - paragraph: "The statement:"
              - generic: task = asyncio.create_task(something()) res = await shield(task)
              - paragraph: "is equivalent to:"
              - generic: res = await something()
              - paragraph:
                - emphasis: except
                - text: that if the coroutine containing it is cancelled, the Task running in
                - code: something()
                - text: is not cancelled. From the point of view of
                - code: something()
                - text: ", the cancellation did not happen. Although its caller is still cancelled, so the “await” expression still raises a"
                - link [ref=f83e683]:
                  - /url: asyncio-exceptions.html#asyncio.CancelledError
                  - code: CancelledError
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - code: something()
                - text: is cancelled by other means (i.e. from within itself) that would also cancel
                - code: shield()
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: If it is desired to completely ignore cancellation (not recommended) the
                - code: shield()
                - text: "function should be combined with a try/except clause, as follows:"
              - generic: "task = asyncio.create_task(something()) try: res = await shield(task) except CancelledError: res = None"
              - generic:
                - paragraph: "Important:"
                - paragraph: Save a reference to tasks passed to this function, to avoid a task disappearing mid-execution. The event loop only keeps weak references to tasks. A task that isn’t referenced elsewhere may get garbage collected at any time, even before it’s done.
              - paragraph:
                - text: "Changed in version 3.10: Removed the"
                - emphasis: loop
                - text: parameter.
