                - emphasis: aw
                - text: is not Future-like object and there is no running event loop.
        - generic:
          - heading [level=2] [ref=f83e703]:
            - link "Timeouts" [ref=f83e704]:
              - /url: "#id11"
          - generic:
            - term:
              - generic: asyncio.
              - generic: timeout
              - text: (
              - emphasis:
                - generic: delay
              - text: )
            - definition:
              - paragraph:
                - text: Return an
                - link "asynchronous context manager" [ref=f83e713]:
                  - /url: ../reference/datamodel.html#async-context-managers
                - text: that can be used to limit the amount of time spent waiting on something.
              - paragraph:
                - emphasis: delay
                - text: can either be
                - code: None
                - text: ", or a float/int number of seconds to wait. If"
                - emphasis: delay
                - text: is
                - code: None
                - text: ", no time limit will be applied; this can be useful if the delay is unknown when the context manager is created."
              - paragraph:
                - text: In either case, the context manager can be rescheduled after creation using
                - link [ref=f83e720]:
                  - /url: "#asyncio.Timeout.reschedule"
                  - code: Timeout.reschedule()
                - text: .
              - paragraph: "Example:"
              - generic: "async def main(): async with asyncio.timeout(10): await long_running_task()"
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - code: long_running_task
                - text: takes more than 10 seconds to complete, the context manager will cancel the current task and handle the resulting
                - link [ref=f83e728]:
                  - /url: asyncio-exceptions.html#asyncio.CancelledError
                  - code: asyncio.CancelledError
                - text: internally, transforming it into a
                - link [ref=f83e730]:
                  - /url: ../builtins/exceptions.html#TimeoutError
                  - code: TimeoutError
                - text: which can be caught and handled.
              - generic:
                - paragraph: "Note:"
                - paragraph:
                  - text: The
                  - link [ref=f83e735]:
                    - /url: "#asyncio.timeout"
                    - code: asyncio.timeout()
                  - text: context manager is what transforms the
                  - link [ref=f83e737]:
                    - /url: asyncio-exceptions.html#asyncio.CancelledError
                    - code: asyncio.CancelledError
                  - text: into a
                  - link [ref=f83e739]:
                    - /url: ../builtins/exceptions.html#TimeoutError
                    - code: TimeoutError
                  - text: ", which means the"
                  - code: TimeoutError
                  - text: can only be caught
